      </div>
      <div class="about-hero-inner">
        <div class="s-label" data-i18n="about.label" style="color:var(--g5)">About The Island GIS</div>
        <h1 class="about-hero-title" data-i18n="about.h1">Built for <em>Cambodian</em><br>GIS Learners</h1>
        <p class="about-hero-body" data-i18n="about.hero.body">The Island GIS was created with one conviction: that the
          gap between a Cambodian GIS
          student and a global geospatial professional is not talent â€” it is access, language, and the right kind of
          teaching.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Story -->
    <div class="story-section">
      <div class="story-inner">
        <div>
          <div class="s-label" data-i18n="story.label">The Story</div>
          <div class="story-pullquote" data-i18n="story.quote">"GIS in Cambodia is mostly still desktop, mostly still
            English, and mostly still
            expensive."</div>
          <p class="story-text" data-i18n="story.text1">That observation sits at the heart of why The Island GIS exists.
            After working across
            humanitarian, government, and research sectors in Cambodia, it became clear that the tools and methods that
            matter most in modern geospatial work â€” Python, Google Earth Engine, cloud analysis, machine learning â€”
            were
            barely taught locally, and almost never in Khmer.</p>
          <p class="story-text" data-i18n="story.text2">The Island GIS was built to close that gap. Not by lowering the
            standard, but by making
            the standard achievable â€” through live teaching in Khmer, research-grounded content, affordable pricing,
            and
            a philosophy that puts the learner's long-term independence above short-term completion.</p>
          <div class="story-highlight">
            <div class="story-highlight-title" data-i18n="story.island.title">Why "The Island"?</div>
            <div class="story-highlight-text" data-i18n="story.island.text">An island is a place you can orient yourself
              from. It sits in the middle
              of something vast â€” like the ocean of geospatial knowledge â€” and gives you a foundation to explore
              outward. The Island GIS is meant to be that foundation: a place you start from, not where you stay.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Philosophy -->
    <div class="philosophy-section">
      <div style="max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto">
        <div class="s-label" style="color:var(--g5)" data-i18n="phil.label">Our Philosophy</div>
        <div class="s-title" style="color:white;margin-top:8px" data-i18n="phil.h1">Four principles we<br>will never
          compromise on</div>
        <div class="philosophy-grid">
          <div class="philosophy-card">
            <div class="philo-num">01</div>
            <div class="philo-title" data-i18n="phil.1.title">Affordable Access</div>
            <div class="philo-text" data-i18n="phil.1.text">Priced for Cambodian realities. Not internationally â€”
              locally. If the price excludes
              a talented student, it is not a good price.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="philosophy-card">
            <div class="philo-num">02</div>
            <div class="philo-title" data-i18n="phil.2.title">Khmer First</div>
            <div class="philo-text" data-i18n="phil.2.text">Complex spatial thinking is clearer in your first language.
              Every live session is in
              Khmer. Slides and code are in English because that is what employers and research communities use.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="philosophy-card">
            <div class="philo-num">03</div>
            <div class="philo-title" data-i18n="phil.3.title">Depth Over Speed</div>
            <div class="philo-text" data-i18n="phil.3.text">We do not rush. We would rather teach fewer topics deeply
              than cover everything
              superficially. A student who truly understands LULC classification is more valuable than one who has run
              every GEE function once.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="philosophy-card">
            <div class="philo-num">04</div>
            <div class="philo-title" data-i18n="phil.4.title">Independence as the Goal</div>
            <div class="philo-text" data-i18n="phil.4.text">The best outcome is not that students keep coming back for
              courses. It is that they
              can learn the next thing on their own, apply it to their own problems, and teach someone else.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Who it's for -->
    <div class="audience-section">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="s-label" data-i18n="aud.label">Who This Is For</div>
        <div class="s-title" data-i18n="aud.h1">If any of these sound like you,<br>you belong here</div>
        <div class="audience-grid">
          <div class="audience-card">
            <div class="audience-icon">ðŸŽ“</div>
            <div class="audience-title" data-i18n="aud.1.title">GIS Students</div>
            <div class="audience-text" data-i18n="aud.1.text">You have learned QGIS or ArcGIS at university and want to
              know how professionals
              actually work â€” with Python, automation, and cloud platforms.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="audience-card">
            <div class="audience-icon">ðŸŒ¿</div>
            <div class="audience-title" data-i18n="aud.2.title">Environment & Land Professionals</div>
            <div class="audience-text" data-i18n="aud.2.text">You work in forestry, agriculture, urban planning, or
              conservation and want to
              use satellite data to do your job better and faster.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="audience-card">
            <div class="audience-icon">ðŸ›</div>
            <div class="audience-title" data-i18n="aud.3.title">Government & NGO Staff</div>
            <div class="audience-text" data-i18n="aud.3.text">You produce spatial reports and maps for decision-makers
              and want to move from
              manual GIS workflows to automated, reproducible analysis.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="audience-card">
            <div class="audience-icon">ðŸ”­</div>
            <div class="audience-title" data-i18n="aud.4.title">Aspiring Researchers</div>
            <div class="audience-text" data-i18n="aud.4.text">You want to publish your own research on Cambodian land,
              climate, or urban
              environments â€” and need the geospatial methods to do it credibly.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>



    <div class="cta-banner">
      <div class="cta-title" data-i18n="cta.about.title">Start your journey with us</div>
      <div class="cta-sub" data-i18n="cta.about.sub">The first cohort is open now. Early bird price: $100 â€” first 10
        registrations.</div>
